                    <div class="reader-page active" id="reader-page-1">
                        <h4>Chapter 1: Decoding Your Skin Type (Fitzpatrick Scale)</h4>
                        <p>The **Fitzpatrick Scale** is the medical standard for classifying human skin coloring and how
                            it reacts to ultraviolet radiation and laser wavelengths. It ranges from Type I (very pale,
                            burns easily) to Type VI (deeply pigmented, never burns).</p>
                        <p>The core problem in mass-volume clinics is the **melanin concentration disparity**. Standard
                            Korean laser protocols are calibrated for local East Asian skin types, which typically hover
                            around Type III and IV.</p>
                        <blockquote>
                            <strong>Why standard settings can be dangerous:</strong>
                            If you possess Type I-II skin, standard settings are often too high, nuking your thin
                            protective barrier and triggering chronic vascular redness or blistering. If you possess
                            Type V-VI skin, active epidermal melanin absorbs the laser heat too quickly, causing
                            permanent laser burns or post-inflammatory hypopigmentation (white spots).
                        </blockquote>
                        <p>Manually adjusting pulse duration and energy fluence for your specific Fitzpatrick type is a
                            fundamental medical necessity—not an optional luxury package.</p>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Chapter 2 -->
                    <div class="reader-page" id="reader-page-2">
                        <h4>Chapter 2: The 5 Questions to Expose a "Skin Factory"</h4>
                        <p>Before allowing a laser to touch your face in Seoul, ignore the front desk sales
                            representatives and demand these answers from the actual performing physician:</p>

                        <!-- Interactive Checklist -->
                        <ul class="safety-checklist">
                            <li class="checklist-item">
                                <div class="checklist-checkbox" onclick="toggleChecklistItem(this)"></div>
                                <div class="checklist-details">
                                    <h5>Q1. "Will the doctor consulting me right now be the exact person performing my
                                        procedure?"</h5>
                                    <p>Exposes shadow-doctor bait-and-switches where sales reps consult and random
                                        practitioners fire lasers.</p>
                                </div>
                            </li>
                            <li class="checklist-item">
                                <div class="checklist-checkbox" onclick="toggleChecklistItem(this)"></div>
                                <div class="checklist-details">
                                    <h5>Q2. "What exact wavelength and pulse duration settings are you using for my
                                        Fitzpatrick type?"</h5>
                                    <p>Verifies if the practitioner understands skin physiology or is simply pressing
                                        automatic presets.</p>
                                </div>
                            </li>
                            <li class="checklist-item">
                                <div class="checklist-checkbox" onclick="toggleChecklistItem(this)"></div>
                                <div class="checklist-details">
                                    <h5>Q3. "Can you show me the genuine, single-use tip packaging and activation log
                                        before we start?"</h5>
                                    <p>Protects you from illegal, reloaded, or counterfeit tips that output unstable
                                        energy spikes.</p>
                                </div>
                            </li>
                            <li class="checklist-item">
                                <div class="checklist-checkbox" onclick="toggleChecklistItem(this)"></div>
                                <div class="checklist-details">
                                    <h5>Q4. "What is your clinic's immediate medical protocol and emergency contact for
                                        burns?"</h5>
                                    <p>Ensures they have real emergency dermatological backup, not just a post-sales
                                        exit strategy.</p>
                                </div>
                            </li>
                            <li class="checklist-item">
                                <div class="checklist-checkbox" onclick="toggleChecklistItem(this)"></div>
                                <div class="checklist-details">
                                    <h5>Q5. "Can I see the practitioner's portfolio/track record with Western skin
                                        profiles?"</h5>
                                    <p>Confirms actual medical experience treating Fitzpatrick Type I-II and V-VI skin
                                        types.</p>
                                </div>
                            </li>
                        </ul>

                        <button id="btnCopyChecklist" onclick="copySafetyChecklist()" class="btn-primary"
